Add a proper prototype for getGpioNum() (defined in examples/blink.c and
wrapped unconditionally by generate-bindings.py) so that wiringpi_wrap.c
does not call it via an implicit declaration. Modern GCC (14+) treats
implicit function declarations as a hard error, which broke the build.

--- a/wiringOP/wiringPi/wiringPi.h
+++ b/wiringOP/wiringPi/wiringPi.h
@@ -896,6 +896,7 @@
 // Internal

 #ifdef CONFIG_ORANGEPI
+extern unsigned char getGpioNum (void);
 extern void piGpioLayoutOops (const char *why);
 #endif

